Just as an addition for other people, who like to use webhooks for Pretix in RocketChat, here is a script, useful to add in the webhook-integrations of Rocket.Chat: 

Step 1: New webhook (fill in everything as you like)
Step 2: Activate script (and please edit [URLOFYOURPRETIXSERVER])

```
class Script {
  process_incoming_request({ request }) {
    // console is a global helper to improve debug
    console.log(request.content);
    return {
      content:{
        attachments: [{
          title: "Ticket " + request.content.code,
          title_link: 'https://[URLOFYOURPRETIXSERVER]/control/event/' + request.content.organizer + "/"+ request.content.event + "/orders/" + request.content.code +"/",
          text: "Bestellung eingegangen",
          fields: [
            {
              title: "Veranstaltung",
              value: request.content.event
            },
            {
              title: "Veranstalter",
              value: request.content.organizer
            }
          ]
        }]
       }
    };
    return {
       error: {
         success: false,
         message: 'Error'
       }
    };
  }
}
```
Step 3: After saving, you will get a webhook-URL, which you have to copy. 
Step 4: Log in to pretix: https:/[URLOFYOURPRETIXSERVER]/control/organizers/ (You need to be admin and organizer for the events you want to add to the webhook). 
Step 5: Add target-webhook-URL. 

Right now, only new orders work well. If someone knows how to deal with the REST-API, more informations can be added to the chatbot, but be careful with personal data you save in the chat (#GDPR).
